  <h2>Squat-Proof Testing Protocol</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Test the actual garment, not only a fabric swatch.</li>
    <li>Check opacity under natural light and strong indoor light.</li>
    <li>Test light colors separately because they can reveal more than black fabric.</li>
    <li>Evaluate the fabric while stretched over the hip and knee areas.</li>
    <li>Repeat the test after washing to confirm shrinkage and recovery.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Waistband and Seam Construction</h2>
  <p>The waistband decides whether leggings feel secure or uncomfortable. A high-rise waistband needs stable recovery, smooth pressure and accurate grading across sizes. Seam choice also matters: flat seams reduce irritation, while poor thread tension can cause puckering or broken stitches during movement.</p>

  <h2>Fit Approval Checklist</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Check waist, hip, inseam, front rise and back rise measurements.</li>
    <li>Try the sample across at least two body types when possible.</li>
    <li>Confirm the waistband does not roll down during movement.</li>
    <li>Inspect crotch seam strength and gusset comfort.</li>
    <li>Wash and remeasure before final approval.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Fitclo Recommendation</h2>
  <p>For premium private label leggings, approve at least two sample rounds: one for fabric and fit direction, and one pre-production sample for final measurements, logo placement, packing and quality standards.</p>
